 and gaseous/particulate polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons during the Ma-tsu Goddess parade</article-title><source>J Expo Anal Environ Epidemiol</source><year>2004</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>536</fpage><lpage>543</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15039797</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.jea.7500372</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lung</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Kao</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Worshippers' exposure to particulate matter in two temples in Taiwan</article-title><source>J Air Waste Manag Assoc</source><year>2003</year><volume>53</volume><fpage>130</fpage><lpage>135</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12617287</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chao</surname><given-names>HR</given-names></name><name><surname>Lin</surname><given-names>TC</given-names></name><name><surname>Hsieh</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Composition and characteristics of PAH emissions from Taiwanese temples</article-title><source>J Aerosol Sci</source><year>1997</year><volume>28  </volume><fpage>s303</fpage><lpage>s304</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0021-8502(97)85152-X</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jetter</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Guo</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>McBrian</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Flynn</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Characterization of emissions from burning incense</article-title><source>Sci Total Environ</source><year>2002</year><volume>295</volume><fpage>51</fpage><lpage>67</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12186292</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0048-9697(02)00043-8</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lin</surname><given-names>TC</given-names></name><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>FH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Burning characteristics and emission products related to metallic content in incense</article-title><source>J Hazard Mater</source><year>2007</year><volume>140</volume><fpage>165</fpage><lpage>172</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16973266</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jhazmat.2006.06.052</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tseng</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name><name><surname>Lin</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><source>Polycyclic Aromatic Hydrocarbons from Burning Raw Materials for a Chinese Incense</source><year>1995</year><volume>Master</volume><publisher-name> National Taiwan University  </publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>USEPA</collab></person-group><article-title>Provisional assessment of recent studies on health effects of particulate matter exposure. (EPA/600/R-06/063)</article-title><year>2006</year></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McDonald</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Ouyang</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Spengler</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Samet</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>McCarthy</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Air Cleaning -- Particles</article-title><s